Caliptra's testbench loads its memory images with $readmemh into memories
shaped `logic [7:0] ram [DEPTH][NUM_BYTES]`, and the files give byte
addresses (`@000231f0`). A file's addresses name words of a memory's highest
dimension (IEEE 1800-2023 21.4.3), so all of `dccm.hex`, and `program.hex`
from its second section on, land past the memory and are not loaded; the ROM
then copies zeros into ICCM and jumps to them. Read each file into a byte
array and copy it into the memory's rows, which loads the same image under
every reading of the address. The same four loads are upstream's, reported as
chipsalliance/caliptra-rtl#1456.

Sent to the suite as https://github.com/verilator/rtlmeter/pull/70

diff --git a/designs/Caliptra/src/caliptra-rtl/caliptra_top_tb_services.sv b/designs/Caliptra/src/caliptra-rtl/caliptra_top_tb_services.sv
index e3abb91..9486664 100644
